From: Ghaf contributors <ghaf@tii.ae>
Subject: [PATCH] daemon: skip config load for users whose home is not their own

cosmic-greeter-daemon assumes each user's identity (run_as_user) before reading
their COSMIC config, so it never reads user files as root. systemd-homed reports
an *inactive* user's home directory as "/" -- the fallback -- because the real
home is an encrypted image that stays unmounted until the user authenticates:

  $ homectl inspect testuser
        State: inactive
    Directory: / (fallback)

So run_as_user() sets HOME=/ and every helper in load_config_as_user() tries to
create /.config as that user. Root owns /, so each one fails with EACCES and the
daemon logs, per such user, on every boot:

  failed to create cosmic-theme mode helper: Io(PermissionDenied)
  failed to create cosmic-theme config helper: Io(PermissionDenied)
  failed to create cosmic-theme builder config helper: Io(PermissionDenied)
  failed to create cosmic-bg state helper: Io(PermissionDenied)
  failed to create cosmic-comp config handler: Permission denied (os error 13)
  failed to create CosmicAppletTime config handler: Io(PermissionDenied)

Nothing is wrong: the config is encrypted and the greeter is not entitled to it
before authentication. An active home is owned by the user, the fallback is not,
so check that before loading. The user still appears on the greeter with the
default theme and wallpaper -- exactly what the failed reads left behind.

Note the check has to be ownership, not readability: "/" is world-readable, so a
readability probe passes and the writes still fail.
---
diff --git a/daemon/src/main.rs b/daemon/src/main.rs
--- a/daemon/src/main.rs
+++ b/daemon/src/main.rs
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 use std::error::Error;
 use std::ffi::CString;
 use std::future::pending;
+use std::os::unix::fs::MetadataExt;
 use std::{env, io};
 use tracing::metadata::LevelFilter;
 use tracing::warn;
@@ -85,6 +86,28 @@
         for user in users {
             let mut user_data = UserData::from(user.clone());
 
+            // systemd-homed reports an INACTIVE user's home as "/" (the
+            // fallback directory), so run_as_user() below would set HOME=/ and
+            // every cosmic_config helper in load_config_as_user() would try to
+            // create /.config as that user. Root owns /, so each one fails with
+            // EACCES and the daemon logs six errors per such user on every boot
+            // -- for config that is still encrypted and unreadable anyway.
+            //
+            // An active home is owned by the user; the fallback is not. Only load
+            // config when we would be reading the user's own directory.
+            let home_is_users = std::fs::metadata(&user.dir)
+                .map(|meta| meta.uid() == user.uid)
+                .unwrap_or(false);
+            if !home_is_users {
+                tracing::debug!(
+                    "skipping config for {}: {:?} is not their home (locked?)",
+                    user.name,
+                    user.dir
+                );
+                user_datas.push(user_data);
+                continue;
+            }
+
             //IMPORTANT: Assume the identity of the user to ensure we don't read user file data as root
             run_as_user(&user, || user_data.load_config_as_user())
                 .map_err(|err| GreeterError::RunAsUser(err.to_string()))?;
